<title>BANGLADESH: Diarrhoea kills nearly 60 Bangladeshis.</title>
<headline>Diarrhoea kills nearly 60 Bangladeshis.</headline>
<dateline>COX'S BAZAR, Bangladesh 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearly 60 people have been killed and over 1,000 infected by diarrhoea in Bangladesh's coastal Cox's Bazar district in the past month, health officials said on Saturday.</p>
<p>They said the disease, caused by people drinking polluted water or eating rotten food, was spreading fast and in several villages there was not a single house without a patient.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a seasonal epidemic and we are trying to contain it as quickly as possible,&quot; one official said.</p>
<p>Local reporters said medical facilities were inadequate to combat the disease.</p>
</text>
